sections.body:
The dictionary has three words for barramundi [ref:hershberger1982]:

- **judi**, marked as the *Yalanji* dialect word, with *murrabal* given as the Nyungkul equivalent;
- **murrabal**, also marked *Yalanji*, but with *kudi* given as the Nyungkul equivalent;
- **kudi**, 'barramundi', with no dialect marked.

The two cross-references do not agree, so the dictionary cannot settle which dialect owns *murrabal*. Speakers of Yalanji and Kuku Nyungkal are the right people to sort it out. Fish in general is **kuyu**, and a good fisherman is **mala-kuyu** [ref:hershberger1982].

**A note for the Mitchell.** The English word 'barramundi' is also one of the common names of the Gulf saratoga (*Scleropages jardinii*), a quite different fish that lives through most of the Gulf of Carpentaria drainage and across northern Queensland [ref:wp-saratoga]. When a Western Yalanji speaker gives you a word for 'barramundi', check which fish they mean.
